HubCli __HUBCLI_VERSION__ (__HUBCLI_TARGET__)
================================================

HubCli is a branded fork of OpenCode (MIT licensed, see LICENSE). It is not
an official product of OpenCode, OpenAI, Anthropic, or NVIDIA.

Install
-------
Unix (macOS/Linux):
  1. Copy this whole directory somewhere permanent, or run install.sh.
  2. Add the directory to your PATH, or symlink ./hubcli into a PATH dir.

Windows:
  1. Copy this whole directory somewhere permanent, or run install.ps1.
  2. Add the directory to your PATH (install.ps1 offers to do this).
  3. Run via hubcli.cmd (or hubcli.ps1 directly from PowerShell).

First use
---------
  hubcli --version
  hubcli --help
  hubcli doctor           # missing providers show as WARN/SKIP, never a crash
  hubcli auth status      # shows which credentials are present (never values)

No provider is required to start HubCli. To add credentials, edit:
  ~/.hubcli/credentials.env        (Unix)
  %USERPROFILE%\.hubcli\credentials.env  (Windows)

Never pass API keys as command-line arguments.

Uninstall
---------
Unix:    bash install.sh --uninstall
Windows: powershell -File install.ps1 -Uninstall

Uninstalling never deletes ~/.hubcli (config, credentials, profiles) unless
you explicitly confirm data removal.

More info: https://github.com/mkvinicius/Hubcli
